      "data": {
        "text": "**Considering Database Choices**\n\nI'm currently focused on selecting a concrete external provider for the NoSQL store. After careful consideration, I've decided to proceed with AWS DynamoDB due to its common usage and widespread adoption. I'll need to make sure this is clearly identifiable within the code of the `fetch_document.py ` script.\n\n\n**Implementing the Fetch Function**\n\nI'm now writing the `fetch_document.py` script. The goal is a function, `fetch_document_by_id`, that retrieves a document from DynamoDB, given a table name and document ID. I'm focusing on making the `boto3` and DynamoDB calls explicit for easy identification and maintenance. Next, I will need to consider how to handle the AWS credentials.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789863997695,
          "start": 1789863996091
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc352abb001MCT97XYXybvGDh",
